  <static seed="1902" source="Contrib/PCC/BasicMath/FractionApplication/MixedNumberMultiplicationWordProblems20.pg">
    <statement><p>A cake recipe needs <m>{1{\textstyle\frac{4}{5}}}</m> cups of flour. Using this recipe, to bake <m>3</m> cakes, how many cups of flour are needed?</p>
<p>To bake <m>3</m> cakes, <fillin characters="9" name="AnSwEr0001"/> cups of flour are needed.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>5{\textstyle\frac{2}{5}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>Each cake needs <m>{1{\textstyle\frac{4}{5}}}</m> cups of flour. To find how many cups of flour are needed to bake <m>3</m> cakes, we use multiplication:</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ 
\begin{aligned}[t]
   {1{\textstyle\frac{4}{5}}} \cdot 3
      \amp = \frac{9}{5} \cdot \frac{3}{1} \\
      
      \amp = \frac{27}{5} \\
      \amp = {5{\textstyle\frac{2}{5}}}
\end{aligned}
    }</m></p>
<p>To bake <m>3</m> cakes, <m>{5{\textstyle\frac{2}{5}}}</m> cups of flour are needed.</p>
</solution>
